{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "g_legend",
      "type": "group",
      "x": -200,
      "y": -1950,
      "width": 2800,
      "height": 300,
      "color": "#8E24AA",
      "label": "COLOR CODING LEGEND & CURRENT STATUS"
    },
    {
      "id": "legend_text",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Biometric Attendance System — visual development map\r\n**Current state:** production firmware workflows IMPLEMENTED; production and compatibility builds pass, 25/25 test environments build; backend API tests pass. R307S is reported silent; hardware and full integration remain unverified.\r\n\r\n🟩 Build/software tests · 🟨 physical tests needed · 🟦 planned UI/API scope · 🟥 safety gates · 🟪 source references",
      "x": -160,
      "y": -1900,
      "width": 2720,
      "height": 220,
      "color": "#8E24AA"
    },
    {
      "id": "g_warnings",
      "type": "group",
      "x": -200,
      "y": -1600,
      "width": 1350,
      "height": 480,
      "color": "#E53935",
      "label": "CRITICAL HARDWARE & ELECTRICAL WARNINGS (RED)"
    },
    {
      "id": "warn_5v",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### ⚠️ ELECTRICAL HAZARD: 3.3V GPIO LIMIT\nESP32 GPIO pins are **NOT 5V tolerant**.\nReported R307S UART wires are already assembled to GPIO32/33; their electrical levels are UNVERIFIED.\nDo not alter connections before checking exact-board mapping, rail and signal voltage with safe equipment.",
      "x": -160,
      "y": -1540,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "#E53935"
    },
    {
      "id": "warn_colors",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### ⚠️ WIRE COLOR ASSUMPTION TRAP\nObserved harness: 1:Red, 2:Black, 3:Yellow, 4:Green, 5:Blue, 6:White.\n**DO NOT ASSUME WIRE COLORS PROVE PINOUT.**\nMany low-cost harnesses insert ribbon cables in arbitrary or reversed order. Always verify ground continuity and silkscreen labels.",
      "x": 490,
      "y": -1540,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "#E53935"
    },
    {
      "id": "warn_battery",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### RTC PRIMARY CELL CAUTION\r\nDS3231 breakout charging circuitry varies by board. Identify the exact breakout and determine whether it charges the backup cell before installing a non-rechargeable CR2032. If uncertain, leave the cell out. Do not assume that changing VCC to 3.3 V disables charging.",
      "x": -160,
      "y": -1310,
      "width": 1270,
      "height": 150,
      "color": "#E53935"
    },
    {
      "id": "g_unverified",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 1220,
      "y": -1600,
      "width": 1380,
      "height": 480,
      "color": "#FFD000",
      "label": "R307S HARDWARE TARGET — UNVERIFIED SPECIFICATIONS (YELLOW)"
    },
    {
      "id": "r307s_module",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### 🟡 R307S Optical Fingerprint Sensor\n- **Physical Status:** Owner reports 6-wire harness assembled: red→VIN, black→GND, yellow→GPIO32, green→GPIO33; blue/white open.\n- **Communication:** Prior diagnostic reportedly returned 0 bytes across baud/routing tests.\n- **Electrical status:** Supply/current, exact PCB pin functions/jumper and signal levels **UNVERIFIED — REQUIRES MULTIMETER / board inspection**.\n- Do not claim the sensor is powered, healthy, or dead.",
      "x": 1260,
      "y": -1540,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "#FFD000"
    },
    {
      "id": "r307s_pins",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### 🟡 Harness Wire Order (Observed)\n- **Pos 1:** Red (Candidate: VCC 4.2V-6V or 3.3V)\n- **Pos 2:** Black (Candidate: GND)\n- **Pos 3:** Yellow (Candidate: TXD out)\n- **Pos 4:** Green (Candidate: RXD in)\n- **Pos 5:** Blue (Candidate: Touch / Wake)\n- **Pos 6:** White (Candidate: 3.3V / NC)\n*All assignments TO VERIFY via multimeter/silkscreen.*",
      "x": 1930,
      "y": -1540,
      "width": 630,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "#FFD000"
    },
    {
      "id": "r307s_uart_spec",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### 🟡 UART & Power Requirements (TO VERIFY)\n- Supply Voltage: Confirm if 5V rail (VIN) or 3.3V direct.\n- TX Logic Level: Measure open-circuit voltage relative to GND (must be <= 3.3V).\n- Default Baud Rate: 57600 baud (provisional default; test ladder if needed).",
      "x": 1260,
      "y": -1310,
      "width": 1300,
      "height": 150,
      "color": "#FFD000"
    },
    {
      "id": "g_verified",
      "type": "group",
      "x": -200,
      "y": -1070,
      "width": 1350,
      "height": 550,
      "color": "#50C878",
      "label": "VERIFIED SUBSYSTEMS & WORKING EVIDENCE (GREEN)"
    },
    {
      "id": "esp32_verified",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### 🟢 ESP32 Microcontroller (Phase 0 PASSED)\n- **Hardware:** ESP32-WROOM-32 DevKit V1.\n- **Port:** Confirmed working on **COM3** at 115200 baud.\n- **Status:** Baseline toolchain test sketch compiled, flashed to hardware, and verified via USB serial output.\n- **Heap & Chip ID:** Reported cleanly in boot telemetry.",
      "x": -160,
      "y": -1010,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 220,
      "color": "#50C878"
    },
    {
      "id": "pio_build_verified",
